            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 5:08 p.m. Eastern Daylight Time Wednesday, Environment Canada has updated a tornado warning for Southwestern Ontario. Extra care and attention should be exercised. The following localities are included in the warning: Perth County, Kitchener, Cambridge and Region of Waterloo. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds and large hail are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
